# PyCharm
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# PyPI configuration file
.pypirc

# Session notes written for restoring context in a later Claude Code session.
# Kept local on purpose: they describe work in progress and reasoning, not the
# state of the code, so they go stale the moment the branch moves on.
history/

# build_campaign_config.py's hours cache lives with the campaign it measures,
# at `projects/ablation-campaign/campaign_hours.json`, and is tracked. It used
# to be ignored here and carried on the campaign-artifacts branch alone, which
# is worth knowing when reading an older checkout.
#
# The rendered `ABL-*.yaml` configs used to be ignored here too, back when they
# were written to `config/train/`. They are tracked now, beside the cache in
# `projects/ablation-campaign/`: a config nobody can see in the diff is a config
# nobody reviews, and being gitignored kept them out of `sync_repo.sh --dirty`
# and silently ran stale renders on the cluster.

# compute_mix_weights.py's measured-hours cache (its --cache default). Unlike
# the campaign cache above it is keyed by absolute shar path, so it is
# machine-specific; keep it locally to make a re-run after adding a corpus
# cheap, but do not track it.
infra/.mix_weights_hours.json

# check_training_config.py's measurement cache (its --cache default). Same
# reasoning: absolute shar paths, so machine-specific. It holds more than the
# hours cache -- per-source cut counts and a duration histogram -- because
# nothing else records those, and re-measuring them is a ~20 minute pass.
infra/.config_check_cache.json

# estimate_bucket_bins.py's per-config output/cache (<config-stem>_bucket_info.json
# and .csv, its --output default). Same reasoning again -- absolute shar paths
# as cache keys -- plus it fully re-derives its own bins on the next
# --force-recompute rather than composing from a durations histogram, so
# there is nothing here worth tracking. Kept out of config/train/ (its
# original default location) so a generated file never looks like part of the
# config a reviewer is meant to read.
infra/.bucket_info/
